  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340898",
      "title": "Handling Request Memoization",
      "lectureOrder": 184,
      "videoOrder": 170,
      "sourceHash": "cee95d9f5225d7c2d34a4f9b187fa82ab19ff995b6605b678f78e2931d422bf2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.9,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "So we have these messages here, which are loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "from that dummy backend, which is a separate process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 11.1,
          "en": "a separate server running in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 14.1,
          "en": "Now, if you open the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "and you go to that window where you start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "at the backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "and you reload this messages page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 23.34,
          "en": "where we see those messages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.34,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "you should see some log messages here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "If you don't, delete this .next folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 32.913,
          "en": "in your NextJS project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 35.83,
          "en": "then quit that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "and restart it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "And most importantly, quit the NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "development server and also restart that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "And then thereafter, in the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.51,
          "en": "where you start at the backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.51,
          "end": 51.18,
          "en": "if you then reload, you should definitely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.18,
          "end": 52.803,
          "en": "see those log messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "And you should see two log messages here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "because in my NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 64.74,
          "en": "I actually got two requests to that backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.74,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "In the messages folder, I have that layout JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "And in there, I have one request to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "where I fetched the messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "And in the page JS file, I got one request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 82.143,
          "en": "So two requests sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "And as you see, these two requests lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "to two request logs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "Now, if you paid close attention,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "this might sound a bit weird",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 96.99000000000001,
          "en": "because I did mention this request memorization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.99000000000001,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "which was a mechanism built into NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 104.553,
          "en": "to avoid duplicate requests to the same data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.96000000000001,
          "end": 109.89,
          "en": "And indeed, here I have one and the same data source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.89,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "one and the same backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "and I'm sending a request to that server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "from two different places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 119.97,
          "en": "And that seems to lead to two different requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "as we can tell by these backend logs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 124.623,
          "en": "And that's exactly what should be avoided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.03,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "And indeed NextJS has a mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "that avoids duplicate requests as we see it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 135.03,
          "en": "But that mechanism is only active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 138.36,
          "en": "if those requests are sent with exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 141.12,
          "en": "the same configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.12,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "And here, I'm talking about requests sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "with the fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "Later, I will also show you how to avoid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "duplicate requests to other data sources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 153.45,
          "en": "like your own database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 155.64,
          "en": "to which you reach out directly from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.64,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "inside the NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 161.25,
          "en": "We can also avoid duplicate requests to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "as you will see later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "But for now, it's about duplicate requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 168.18,
          "en": "to a separate backend, which we clearly have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.18,
          "end": 170.73,
          "en": "And we have those duplicate requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.73,
          "end": 172.56,
          "en": "because the request I sent here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.56,
          "end": 174.63,
          "en": "in the messages page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.63,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "and the request I send in the messages layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "are not exactly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 182.73,
          "en": "They have a different headers configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.73,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "and I set up this different configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "so that on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "I can log which exact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "place in the front end did send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "I'm extracting that headers data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 198.03,
          "en": "and I'm logging it here, but therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.03,
          "end": 201.273,
          "en": "I have different requests with different configurations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "Now, what you will see is that if I get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "of this headers configuration in my NextJS application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "here in the messages page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "and then also, in the messages layout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 216.96,
          "en": "and I then save the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 216.96,
          "end": 218.91,
          "en": "I have exactly the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.91,
          "end": 222.12,
          "en": "request signature in both places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 222.12,
          "end": 225.39,
          "en": "And if I do that and I then go to my backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 225.39,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "again, you can already see that only one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 230.523,
          "en": "new request was added to it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 234.63,
          "en": "Now, if I reload this messages page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 238.14,
          "en": "you will see that actually no new request is sent here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 240.573,
          "en": "And I'll get back to why that's the case later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.68,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "You can always delete this .next folder though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "to reset the NextJS application essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 251.94,
          "en": "because that .next folder holds some temporary data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 255.42,
          "en": "some cache data that's used by the next application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.42,
          "end": 257.04,
          "en": "And if you delete that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.04,
          "end": 260.55,
          "en": "and then restart the next development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.55,
          "end": 263.25,
          "en": "it will be recreated with fresh data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 264.6,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "and you go to that backend page again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.95,
          "en": "you will see that now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 268.95,
          "end": 272.7,
          "en": "if I maybe also restart that to clear the logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 276.9,
          "en": "that now, if I reload that messages page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.9,
          "end": 279.513,
          "en": "only one new request is added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 284.64,
          "en": "And keep in mind that earlier we had two requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 284.64,
          "end": 286.89,
          "en": "one from the layout, one from the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.89,
          "end": 289.56,
          "en": "Now, since I'm not sending those extra headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 289.56,
          "end": 292.23,
          "en": "which were different anymore, I can't tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.23,
          "end": 295.53,
          "en": "where this request is coming from, but I can tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 298.44,
          "en": "that it's only one request instead of two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.44,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "So that's that request memorization in action here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "And that's one key mechanism built into NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 308.76,
          "en": "which you get for free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.76,
          "end": 310.98,
          "en": "Whenever you have two requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.98,
          "end": 313.38,
          "en": "with exactly the same configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.38,
          "end": 318.12,
          "en": "In this case here, fetch requests sent to a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 321.51,
          "en": "NextJS avoids unnecessary requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 323.7,
          "en": "and instead just sends one request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 323.7,
          "end": 326.55,
          "en": "and then reuses the response in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 329.283,
          "en": "of the application that needs the response.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
